RefineryRelay is installed.

Next steps:
  1. Set RELAY_CHAT_BASE_URL, RELAY_CHAT_TOKEN, RELAY_CHAT_TENANT_KEY,
     RELAY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL, RELAY_RSS_FEED_URL, RELAY_SOURCE_TOKEN,
     and REDIS_URL in the host environment.
  2. Restart the Rails application so the initializer and Pod registration load.
  3. In Refinery admin, create an LLM Chat Pod and add it to a page.
  4. Run `bin/rails db:migrate` to enable the site-wide Styling settings and per-pod Chat content.
  5. Verify the availability endpoint and submit a browser chat request.

Chat endpoints:
  GET  /refinery_relay/api/relay/chat/availability
  POST /refinery_relay/api/relay/chat

Source endpoint (provided automatically by the gem):
  GET  /refinery_relay/api/relay/documents

The installer can be run again safely; existing host configuration is preserved.
